lisa-design:
- Exact (solid) links: an event whose data.effect equals the spec.idempotencyKey of an action's rule effect or of one of its task's effects (taskEffects). Run completions stay solid too. All exact links are computed before any inferred one.
- The heuristic now skips events that some effect is exactly linked to, so an action never gets an inferred link to an event already linked exactly (from it or another action); it still picks the next factory event on the same object, e.g. a push's pr.updated or a pr.labeled, which name no effect. Reading "only for actions that have no exact link" strictly would drop the push -> pr.updated case the brief gives as its example, so it is per event, not per action.
- Mock: the pipeline's pr.opened carries data.effect = implement's pr.open key (exact); a new rule label-factory-prs labels docs#78 and GitHub's pr.labeled names no effect (inferred, from both actions touching docs#78). The new decision is appended last so earlier decision indices don't move.

